    "show_share": true,
    "description": "After sixteen years of exemplary leadership of the Board of Trustees, former Minister for Foreign Affairs, Sahabzada Yaqub-Khan, Chairman of the Board of Aga Khan University (AKU), stepped down in accordance with his wishes and with the approval of the Chancellor, His Highness the Aga Khan. At a banquet in his honour, hosted by the Chancellor, on the occasion of the meetings of the Board of Trustees in Paris, the Chancellor recalled the vital role Sahabzada Yaqub-Khan played in steering the University through its early days, overcoming numerous challenges with his exceptional qualities of leadership and diplomacy.  AKU today is known nationally and internationally for the quality of its teaching, research and service.",
